  "ownership": "Single private X connection owns borrowed RandR metadata and event registrations. Every metadata reply is freed; the fixed 256-sample array remains on the stack; request counters retain no handles. Damage/region and cursor subscriptions settle on that original connection before XCloseDisplay; no RGB/VA/DRM import is made by the measurement. Existing lifecycle fixtures separately preserve original copy/fence/lease rejection oracles. Xvfb wrappers settle before output collection, with no elapsed execution cap.",
  "scope": "Three trials for each of two identity modes: 1536 layout-check pairs, 1536 pointer samples, 30 idle waits. Native X requests/latency on isolated 128x128 software Xvfb, not physical compositor/GPU/power/CPU acceptance. Initial build smoke measurements excluded from trial results.",
  "interpretation": "Production EDID path emits ten requests per pair and zero additional successful atom-lookup requests after initialization. Name-only fixture has no EDID atom: its 256 absent-atom lookups each send a request; that separate diagnostic is outside the measured layout pair. Pointer samples each emit one request; all 30 idle waits emit 26 pointer queries. Timings include instrumentation overhead and host scheduling; no end-to-end speedup inferred.",
  "limitations": "No hardware or installed session changed. Native acceptance retained in T1724. T1722 tracks the capped coverage runner; finite source cases were compiled/executed directly without its timeout. T1723 tracks historical benchmark extraction; measurements compile current sources directly. Nonessential benchmark coverage exemption applies; no production functions changed."
}
